module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.LocalizationCompletionFiniteType
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.PushforwardCommutesCompletion

/-!
# The comparison map of Tag 0A0G restricts to the comparison map of the localized morphism

Let `f : (Sh(𝒟), 𝒪') ⟶ (Sh(𝒞), 𝒪)` be a morphism of ringed sites, let `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪` and `ℐ' ⊂ 𝒪'` be
sheaves of ideals with `f^♯(f^{-1}ℐ) ⊂ ℐ'`, and let `V` be an object of `𝒞`, with `U = u(V)`.
[Stacks, Tag 0A0G] has a canonical comparison map
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison`,
`(Rf_*K)^∧ ⟶ Rf_*(K^∧)`, and the localized morphism `f' : (Sh(𝒟/U), 𝒪'_U) ⟶ (Sh(𝒞/V), 𝒪_V)` of
[Stacks, Tag 04J0] has its own, for the restricted sheaves of ideals. This file proves that the
two agree: restricting the comparison map of `f` to `𝒞/V` gives the comparison map of `f'`.

This is what makes the invertibility of the comparison map a **local** question on the target
site, which is how [Stacks, Tag 0A0G] is reached at a sheaf of ideals that is only locally
generated by finitely many sections: `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.IsFinitelyGeneratedOver`
holds on a covering family, and the comparison map is invertible there.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedPushforwardOverIso`: **`Rf_*` commutes with restriction
  to a slice site**, that is [Stacks, Tag 0D6G] written with `Functor.mapDerivedCategory` in
  place of the right derived functor `derivedRestriction`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.pushforwardIdealCompatible_localized`: the relation
  `f^♯(f^{-1}ℐ) ⊂ ℐ'` of [Stacks, Tag 099J] restricts to the localized morphism and the
  restricted sheaves of ideals.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison_localized`: **the
  restriction coherence**, as a commuting square: the comparison map of `f` restricted to
  `𝒞/V`, conjugated by the two comparison maps of [Stacks, Tag 0A0F] and by
  `derivedPushforwardOverIso`, is the comparison map of `f'`.

## Implementation notes

*Why the proof is in term mode.* The two spellings of the category of sheaves of modules on a
slice — `SheafOfModules (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).over U)`, in which
[Stacks, Tag 0D6G] and `Stacks.Cohomology.Localization.derivedRestriction` are stated, and
`SheafOfModules ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (X.over U).O))`, in which
`derivedCompletion` is — are definitionally equal but receive *different* `Abelian` instances
from instance search, and hence different `DerivedCategory`s. The statement below therefore mixes
them, and is type-correct only at default transparency. That is enough for `exact`, and not
enough for `rw`: every rewrite in the square fails, because `rw` builds its motive at a reduced
transparency at which the goal is not type-correct. So the chase is written as a chain of
`Eq.trans` and `congrArg`, where each step is checked by unification at default transparency.
The two steps that do need a rewrite — functoriality of restriction and of `Rf'_*` applied to a
composite — are isolated into `have`s whose statements are written here in a single spelling,
where the rewrite does fire.

*The shape of the chase.* Both sides of the square are maps out of the derived completion of
`(Rf_*K)|_V` along `ℐ|_V`, and the target `Rf'_*((K^∧)|_U)` is derived complete along `ℐ|_V` —
it is the direct image along `f'` of an object derived complete along `ℐ'|_U`, by
[Stacks, Tag 099J] for `f'`. So the two sides are equal as soon as their composites with the
completion map agree, by `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.hom_ext_derivedCompletionUnit`. Each
composite reduces, by the defining property of the three comparison maps, to
`σ ∘ Rf'_*(η|_U)` where `η : K ⟶ K^∧` is the completion map and `σ` is
`derivedPushforwardOverIso`; the two reductions meet at the naturality of `σ` applied to `η`.

Note that only the *naturality* of [Stacks, Tag 0D6G] is used, not its unit compatibility
(`pushforwardRestrictionUnit_comp_derivedPushforwardOverFunctorIso_hom_app`):
the comparison maps of [Stacks, Tag 0A0F] already carry their own unit compatibilities, and
those are what the chase consumes.

*Transporting invertibility.* For sheaves of ideals of finite type the other three edges of the
square are invertible: the two comparison maps of [Stacks, Tag 0A0F] by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_derivedCompletionRestrictComparison_overIdeal_app`, and
`derivedPushforwardOverIso` by construction. So the square transports invertibility of the
comparison map in both directions, which is what makes [Stacks, Tag 0A0G] a local question on the
target site. That transport is deliberately *not* packaged as a lemma here: it has to be done at the
consumer's own spelling of the category of sheaves of modules on a slice. In this module's mixed
spelling (see above) `IsIso` of either composite is not synthesizable by instance search, because
the two `≫`s carry definitionally equal but syntactically distinct `DerivedCategory` instances and
instance search matches only up to reducible transparency. A consumer that has fixed one spelling
gets the transport from `CategoryTheory.isIso_comp_left_iff` and
`CategoryTheory.isIso_comp_right_iff` in two lines.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 099J](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099J)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0G](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0G)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0D6G](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0D6G)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 04J0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04J0)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite
open Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedPullbackPushforwardAdjunction
open Stacks.Cohomology.Localization

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

attribute [local instance 100000] HasDerivedCategory.standard
attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.hasSheafCompose_forget₂_ringCat

variable {X Y : RingedSite.{u, u, u}} (f : RingedSite.Hom X Y) (V : Y.C)
  (I : SheafOfModules.Submodule
    (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))))
  (I' : SheafOfModules.Submodule
    (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))))

/-- **`Rf_*` commutes with restriction to a slice site**, written with
`CategoryTheory.Functor.mapDerivedCategory` rather than with the right derived functor
`Stacks.Cohomology.Localization.derivedRestriction`.

This is [Stacks, Tag 0D6G], `Stacks.Cohomology.Localization.derivedPushforwardOverFunctorIso`,
conjugated on both sides by `Stacks.Cohomology.Localization.derivedRestrictionIso`, which
identifies the degreewise restriction of complexes with its own right derived functor because
restriction is exact. It is the form in which the derived completion machinery — stated with
`mapDerivedCategory` throughout — can consume the tag. -/
def derivedPushforwardOverIso :
    derivedPushforward.{u} f.toRingedToposSiteHom ⋙
        (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))
          V).mapDerivedCategory ≅
      (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
        (f.u.obj V)).mapDerivedCategory ⋙
        derivedPushforward.{u} (f.localized V).toRingedToposSiteHom :=
  Functor.isoWhiskerLeft _ (derivedRestrictionIso Y V) ≪≫
    derivedPushforwardOverFunctorIso f V ≪≫
    Functor.isoWhiskerRight (derivedRestrictionIso X (f.u.obj V)).symm _

/-- **The relation of [Stacks, Tag 099J] between two sheaves of ideals restricts to a slice
site.** If `f^♯` carries `f^{-1}ℐ` into `ℐ'`, then the structure map of the localized morphism
of [Stacks, Tag 04J0] carries `(f')^{-1}(ℐ|_V)` into `ℐ'|_U`.

This is immediate: a section of `ℐ|_V` over an object `W` of `𝒞/V` *is* a section of `ℐ` over
`W.left`, the structure map of the localized morphism is the restriction of `f^♯`
(`Stacks.Cohomology.Localization.fSharpRing_localized`), and `u'(W).left = u(W.left)`. -/
theorem pushforwardIdealCompatible_localized (hI : PushforwardIdealCompatible f I I') :
    PushforwardIdealCompatible (f.localized V) (overIdeal I V) (overIdeal I' (f.u.obj V)) :=
  fun W s hs => hI W.left s hs

variable (hI : PushforwardIdealCompatible f I I')
  [(ObjectProperty.ι (IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} Y I)).IsRightAdjoint]
  [(ObjectProperty.ι (IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X I')).IsRightAdjoint]
  [(ObjectProperty.ι (IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} (Y.over V) (overIdeal I V))).IsRightAdjoint]
  [(ObjectProperty.ι (IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} (X.over (f.u.obj V))
      (overIdeal I' (f.u.obj V)))).IsRightAdjoint]

/-- **The comparison map of [Stacks, Tag 0A0G] restricted to a slice site is the comparison map
of the localized morphism**, as a commuting square.

Going along the top: the comparison map of [Stacks, Tag 0A0F] for `ℐ` on `𝒞/V`, then the
restriction to `𝒞/V` of the comparison map of `f`, then `derivedPushforwardOverIso`. Going
round the bottom: `derivedPushforwardOverIso` completed, then the comparison map of the
localized morphism `f'`, then the comparison map of [Stacks, Tag 0A0F] for `ℐ'` on `𝒟/U`
pushed forward along `f'`. Both are maps `((Rf_*K)|_V)^∧ ⟶ Rf'_*((K^∧)|_U)`.

Both sides are determined by their composite with the completion map of `(Rf_*K)|_V`, because
the common target is derived complete along `ℐ|_V`; the two composites both reduce to
`derivedPushforwardOverIso` followed by `Rf'_*` of the restricted completion map of `K`, and
meet at the naturality of `derivedPushforwardOverIso`. -/
theorem derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison_localized
    (K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))) :
    (derivedCompletionRestrictComparison Y I V (overIdeal I V) (fun _ _ h => h)).app
          ((derivedPushforward.{u} f.toRingedToposSiteHom).obj K) ≫
        (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))
          V).mapDerivedCategory.map
          ((derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison f I I' hI).app K) ≫
        (derivedPushforwardOverIso f V).hom.app ((derivedCompletion X I').obj K) =
      (derivedCompletion (Y.over V) (overIdeal I V)).map
            ((derivedPushforwardOverIso f V).hom.app K) ≫
        (derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison (f.localized V) (overIdeal I V)
            (overIdeal I' (f.u.obj V))
            (pushforwardIdealCompatible_localized f V I I' hI)).app
          ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
            (f.u.obj V)).mapDerivedCategory.obj K) ≫
        (derivedPushforward.{u} (f.localized V).toRingedToposSiteHom).map
          ((derivedCompletionRestrictComparison X I' (f.u.obj V) (overIdeal I' (f.u.obj V))
            (fun _ _ h => h)).app K) := by
  have h1 : (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))
      V).mapDerivedCategory.map
          ((derivedCompletionUnit Y I).app
            ((derivedPushforward.{u} f.toRingedToposSiteHom).obj K)) ≫
        (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))
          V).mapDerivedCategory.map
          ((derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison f I I' hI).app K) =
      (SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))
        V).mapDerivedCategory.map
        ((derivedPushforward.{u} f.toRingedToposSiteHom).map
          ((derivedCompletionUnit X I').app K)) := by
    rw [← Functor.map_comp,
      derivedCompletionUnit_comp_derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison f I I' hI]
  have h2 : (derivedPushforward.{u} (f.localized V).toRingedToposSiteHom).map
          ((derivedCompletionUnit (X.over (f.u.obj V)) (overIdeal I' (f.u.obj V))).app
            ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
              (f.u.obj V)).mapDerivedCategory.obj K)) ≫
        (derivedPushforward.{u} (f.localized V).toRingedToposSiteHom).map
          ((derivedCompletionRestrictComparison X I' (f.u.obj V)
            (overIdeal I' (f.u.obj V)) (fun _ _ h => h)).app K) =
      (derivedPushforward.{u} (f.localized V).toRingedToposSiteHom).map
        ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
          (f.u.obj V)).mapDerivedCategory.map
          ((derivedCompletionUnit X I').app K)) := by
    rw [← Functor.map_comp,
      derivedCompletionUnit_comp_derivedCompletionRestrictComparison X I' (f.u.obj V)
        (overIdeal I' (f.u.obj V)) (fun _ _ h => h)]
  refine hom_ext_derivedCompletionUnit (Y.over V) (overIdeal I V)
    (derivedPushforward_isDerivedComplete (f.localized V) (overIdeal I V)
      (overIdeal I' (f.u.obj V)) (pushforwardIdealCompatible_localized f V I I' hI) _
      (isDerivedComplete_derivedRestrict_derivedCompletion X I' (f.u.obj V)
        (overIdeal I' (f.u.obj V)) (fun _ _ h => h) K)) ?_
  trans (derivedPushforwardOverIso f V).hom.app K ≫
      (derivedPushforward.{u} (f.localized V).toRingedToposSiteHom).map
        ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
          (f.u.obj V)).mapDerivedCategory.map
          ((derivedCompletionUnit X I').app K))
  · exact (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm.trans
      ((congrArg (· ≫ _) (derivedCompletionUnit_comp_derivedCompletionRestrictComparison
            Y I V (overIdeal I V) (fun _ _ h => h) _)).trans
        ((Category.assoc _ _ _).symm.trans
          ((congrArg (· ≫ _) h1).trans
            ((derivedPushforwardOverIso f V).hom.naturality _))))
  · exact (congrArg (_ ≫ ·) h2.symm).trans
      ((congrArg (fun m => _ ≫ (m ≫ _))
            (derivedCompletionUnit_comp_derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison
              (f.localized V) (overIdeal I V) (overIdeal I' (f.u.obj V))
              (pushforwardIdealCompatible_localized f V I I' hI) _).symm).trans
        ((congrArg (_ ≫ ·) (Category.assoc _ _ _)).trans
          ((Category.assoc _ _ _).symm.trans
            ((congrArg (· ≫ _) ((derivedCompletionUnit (Y.over V)
                  (overIdeal I V)).naturality _)).trans (Category.assoc _ _ _)))))

end AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

end
